spec:
  grid: 10-15 rows x 12-17 cols
  colors: bg=0, marker=2 [observed], wall=8 [observed]; exactly 2 foreground colors
  marker:
    single cell on exactly one grid edge (non-corner)
    parallel-axis position roughly 0.3-0.5 of that dimension [observed]
  wall_lines:
    3-4 parallel lines perpendicular to marker's inward direction
    each line spans full grid width/height (edge-to-edge) with 1-3 single-cell gaps
    wall coverage per line >=70% of the line length
    gap size always exactly 1 cell
    spacing between consecutive lines: 2-4 cells
    distance from marker edge to nearest line: 2-3 cells
    distance from farthest line to opposite edge: 2-4 cells
  constraint: marker's inward ray always hits a wall segment (not a gap) on the first line
  output:
    walls preserved unchanged
    marker color painted along every cell visited by branching inward traversal
    traversal branches at each wall-segment's endpoints (the 1-cell openings beside the hit segment)
    branching depth 2-4, total branches 3-9

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims, marker edge (top/bottom/left/right), and number of wall lines (3-4).
    2. Place wall lines at increasing distances from marker edge (first at 2-3, gaps of 2-4).
    3. For each wall line, fill the full span with wall color, then remove 1-3 single-cell gaps at random positions (not at grid edges; ensure gap positions are interior).
    4. Choose marker position on its edge such that its inward column/row intersects a wall segment (not a gap) on the first wall line.
    5. Run the solver to produce the output and verify branching depth >=2 and total branches >=3. Reject trivial outputs (e.g. straight line with no branching).
```
